.TH APPATTIC\-QT 1 "2026-10-02" "appattic-qt 3.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
appattic\-qt \- Qt 6 window for leftover, stale app, package and disk scans
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B appattic-qt
.RB [ --version ]
.RB [ --help ]
.RB [ --smoke ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B appattic\-qt
is the Linux window of AppAttic. It shows leftovers from uninstalled apps,
stale installed apps, outdated versions, unused distro and language packages,
and disk usage. Nothing is deleted until a script is reviewed in the window
or the move is confirmed.
.PP
Package-manager queries run on the host. As a Flatpak they are spawned with
.B flatpak-spawn --host
and plugin tags are read from
.IR /run/host ;
installed as a plain CMake or AppImage package they run directly. Scan plugins
cannot delete files or run a distro upgrade.
.PP
The WASM modules are read from
.IR $APPATTIC_CORE_OUT ,
or from
.I ../share/appattic
next to the binary.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR --help ", " \-h
Print a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B --smoke
Run the headless smoke test and exit. Prints
.B SMOKE=ok
on success. Useful with
.B QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen
on a host with no display server.
.TP
.BI --dev-check " check" " [dir]"
Debug build only. Run one gate and exit:
.BR table ", " overview ", " stream ", " disk ", or " shot
(the page renders go to
.IR dir ).
The gate is compiled out of a release build, which rejects the option with
exit 2 rather than opening the window. A gate name outside that list is
rejected with exit 2 before the window is built.
.PP
An unknown
.B \-\-option
is reported by name and exits 2, rather than opening the window and running
nothing. Qt's own options are single-dash, so
.BI \- platform " name"
and the rest still pass through.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B APPATTIC_CORE_OUT
Directory holding the compiled WASM modules. Unset or empty searches
.I ../share/appattic
and the build output directories next to the binary.
.TP
.B APPATTIC_HOST_EXEC_LIVE
.B 1
runs the core's allowlisted package queries against the real binaries instead
of the built-in fixtures. Off by default, and read as off for any value other
than
.BR 1 ,
.BR true ,
.BR yes ,
or
.BR on .
.TP
.B APPATTIC_HOST_EXEC_FIXTURE
.B 1
serves the built-in fixtures on non-macOS hosts. Same accepted values as
.BR APPATTIC_HOST_EXEC_LIVE .
macOS uses fixtures either way.
.TP
.B APPATTIC_PAGE
Initial sidebar page:
.BR overview ,
.BR leftovers ,
.BR stale ,
.BR outdated ,
.BR packages ,
.BR disk ,
or
.BR settings .
An unset or empty value opens the overview; an unknown name is reported on
stderr and also opens the overview.
.TP
.B FLATPAK_ID
Set by Flatpak. Any non-empty value means the app is sandboxed, so plugin tags
and package-manager queries go through
.I /run/host
and
.BR flatpak-spawn --host .
Unset or empty is a normal host run.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Absolute data root. Parent of
.I appattic/settings.json
and
.IR appattic/last-scan.json .
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Absolute configuration root scanned for leftovers and usage history.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Absolute cache root scanned for leftovers.
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Absolute state root scanned for leftovers.
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Session runtime root, read for the
.I gvfs
directory the network-folder disk scan opens at. Unset, empty, relative, or
naming a root with no
.I gvfs
in it uses
.IR ~/.gvfs .
.TP
.B WASMTIME_DIR
Wasmtime C API prefix used at build time, not at run time.
.PP
Per the XDG Base Directory specification, an empty or relative XDG path is
ignored and the standard user default is used. The accepted values and their
effects are the same ones
.B appattic config
prints.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The window closed normally, or the requested option completed.
.TP
.B 1
The scan failed, or the smoke test failed.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error: an option this build does not take, or a gate name it does not
know.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/appattic/settings.json
Confirm-before-running and ignored leftover paths. Include-system-apps is a macOS-only setting; the Linux window does not scan installed system apps. A missing file uses the defaults. A file that is malformed, or whose
.I ignoredLeftoverPaths
entry is not the full path a report prints, is named in an error and left unoverwritten, and the window opens with no settings until it is corrected.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/appattic/settings.json.bak
The settings file as it was before the last change, written owner-only by every
settings save that changed the file. It is what the window's "Restore settings
from backup" puts back, and
.B appattic restore
puts back from the command line, after checking it loads. Nothing reads it while
the window runs.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/appattic/settings.json.bad
The settings file a restore replaced, kept so a restore that turns out to be the
wrong one is not a second loss. Nothing reads it while the window runs, and
.B appattic erase
leaves it. The procedure is
.IR docs/runbooks/state-recovery.md .
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/appattic/last-scan.json
The scan cache, a full list of the app and leftover paths the last scan found
under your home directory. It is owner-only. A run that removes or updates
something drops it, so the next run scans again, and so does a run more than 24
hours after the one that wrote it.
.B appattic erase
removes it on demand, whatever its age, and reports on standard output whether
there was one, so the result is pipeable like every other command's.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/AppAttic/AppAttic.conf
Settings the window used before
.I settings.json
existed. They are copied over the first time the window starts without one, and
a copy that lands in
.I settings.json
deletes this file, because the ignore list it holds is then in the new file and
nothing opens this one again. A migration that could not be written leaves it,
since it is then the only copy. A value there that is neither true nor false is
not copied: the window names the key and this file, and opens with no settings
until you correct it. Delete it to start from the defaults.
.TP
.I ../share/appattic/licenses
License text for the third-party files compiled into the binary, such as the
SIL OFL 1.1 grant for the Michroma title font.
.SH SEE ALSO
The project README and
.I https://github.com/maci0/appattic
for the full scan description.
